  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader on the iPhone Duo in landscape, I want the reader's controls to stay put when I reach the bottom of a page, so that nothing blinks under my thumb. Operator feedback, 2026-11-27 (two screenshots, kept off the tracker: they show real members' posts).\n\n### Observed (operator's iPhone Duo, landscape, dark, topic reader)\n- Reaching the **bottom of a topic page**, a zone at the bottom of the reader shows **ghost, half-drawn controls**: round buttons and a page-number pill, blurred over the last message's signature.\n- At the same time the **side rail** on the right shows **empty capsules** where its buttons should be.\n- The controls **blink** between the two places: the layout seems to hesitate between bottom controls and the side rail. Likely tied to the side rail of the landscape layout.\n\n### Expected (operator)\n- **Keep the page number at the bottom** (the page pill).\n- The other controls stay in one place (the side rail in landscape), with no flicker and no ghost buttons.\n\n### To check\nThe bottom bar's visibility rule at the end of the page (scroll-edge / reached-bottom state) against the landscape rail's: two views probably claim the same controls and toggle on each scroll or layout pass. Related: #1417 (floating refresh over the last message), #1418 (duplicate refresh on the rail): same screen, same layout; fix together if the cause is shared.\n\n### Acceptance\n- On the Duo in landscape (and the other sizes), scrolling to the end of a page keeps the page pill at the bottom and every other control on the rail, with no blinking; a hosted test or snapshot pins the end-of-page state.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
